@startuml
title Student Attendance System - Domain Model
hide methods
hide circle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class "User" as User <<entity>> {
  full name
  role: administrator / lecturer / student
  student number or staff ID
}
class "Course" as Course <<entity>> {
  course code
  course name
}
class "Enrollment" as Enrollment <<entity>> {
  enrollment date and time
}
class "Lecture Session" as Session <<entity>> {
  session date and start/end time
  active status
  allowed attendance radius
}
class "Attendance Record" as Attendance <<entity>> {
  scan date and time
  attendance status
  distance from lecturer
}
class "Mobile Location Request" as Request <<entity>> {
  proposed session date and time
  setup token and expiry
  status: pending / completed / expired / used
}
class "Attendance QR" as QR <<value object>> {
  session link and token
  expiry
}
class "Geographic Location" as Location <<value object>> {
  latitude
  longitude
  reported accuracy: optional
}

User "1" -- "0..*" Course : teaches {lecturer}
User "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : holds {student}
Course "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : receives
Course "1" -- "0..*" Session : schedules
User "1" -- "0..*" Session : creates {lecturer}
User "1" -- "0..*" Attendance : submits {student}
Session "1" -- "0..*" Attendance : records
User "1" -- "0..*" Request : initiates {lecturer}
Course "1" -- "0..*" Request : prepares attendance for
Session "1" -- "1" QR : offers
Session "1" --> "0..1" Location : lecturer position
Attendance "1" --> "1" Location : student position
Request "1" --> "0..1" Location : captured phone position

note top of User
Administrator, lecturer and student are user roles.
Administrators manage users, courses and enrollments,
and review attendance across the system.
end note
note bottom of Enrollment
An enrollment connects one student to one course.
The student must be enrolled by session creation time
to submit attendance for that session.
end note
note bottom of Attendance
One accepted submission per student per session.
Requires an active session, valid unexpired QR token,
lecturer position and student within the allowed radius.
New sessions allow 50 meters; QR tokens last 15 minutes.
end note
note bottom of Request
Optional mobile setup, with a 5-minute token lifetime.
Completed coordinates are copied into session creation.
The frontend then marks the request used.
end note
note bottom of Location
A value describing a position, not a shared location entity.
Each association represents a separate position value.
The frontend checks student accuracy <= 50 meters;
the API separately checks distance from the lecturer.
end note

legend bottom
  Business concepts and intended multiplicities, inferred from the application.
  QR and location are conceptual values, not additional database tables.
  Session QR images are generated from the stored session token and frontend URL.
  Credentials, database IDs, foreign-key fields and controller methods are omitted.
  Database constraints cannot be verified without the missing schema/migrations.
endlegend
@enduml
